# No em dashes

Never write an em dash (`—`) or the HTML entity `&mdash;`. This is a hard ban in user-facing copy, system prompts, ticket text, comments, and commit messages.

Do not use an en dash (`–`) as a substitute for a pause. En dashes are only for numeric ranges that already exist in source (`3–5`). Prefer `3-5` in new copy.

Replace a pause with a period, a comma, or a colon.

```
# BAD
Hi Liam — I have your account.
Stay here — their reply will land here.

# GOOD
Hi Liam. I have your account.
Stay here. Their reply will land here.
```

If you find an existing em dash while editing a file, remove it in the same change.
